.git/
.github/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pyright/
# `**/`, because a bare pattern in this file matches at the root of the
# context and nowhere below it. Until 2026-09-13 these two lines were bare, and
# the image carried 441 `.pyc` files local test runs had written under `src/`,
# 84 of them for a Python 3.13 the image does not have. Since the project's
# `uv sync` sits right after `COPY src`, a test run would also re-run it on
# the next build without a line of code having changed.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.secrets/
API key/
api-key/
*.key
var/
artifacts/
build/
dist/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/coverage/
web/playwright-report/
web/test-results/
htmlcov/
.coverage
tests/
docs/
evals/
# Except the reports `EvaluationPage.test.tsx` imports at build time, so the
# page cannot drift from the repository. Excluding them does not omit them from
# the image, it stops the image from building at all (TS2307 under `tsc -b`,
# which compiles the tests too).
#
# It is the *test* that imports them, not `reports.ts` -- the page reads the
# directory over HTTP. This comment said otherwise until 2026-08-31, which would
# have sent whoever deleted that test looking for an import that is not there.
!evals/rag/reports/dense-llama_index.json
!evals/rag/reports/dense-reference.json
!evals/rag/reports/hybrid-llama_index.json
!evals/rag/reports/hybrid-reference.json
!evals/chat/reports/chat-hybrid-180s.json
!evals/triage/reports/report.json
*.md~
.DS_Store
